<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27092" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δίν-η</span></b> , ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>whirlpool, eddy,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				21.213
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Eu.</u>
				559
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Tr.</u>
				210
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Cra.</u>
				439c
			</span></i>, etc.: pl., <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				21.353
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Th.</u>
				791
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				2.28
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὶ Κυανέας δ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>CIG</u>
					3797
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="entity">Chalcedon</span>): generally, of the sea, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τυρσηνὶς δ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					9.308
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="entity">Bianor</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of the <i>rotating heaven,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Emp.
				35.4
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰθέρος δῖναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					115.11
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Phd.</u>
				99b
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Cael.</u>
				295a13
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ph.</u>
				196a26
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>whirlwind,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Av.</u>
				697
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δῖναι νεφέλας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Alc.</u>
					244
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			generally, <i>circular motion, rotation,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Av.</u>
				1198
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀτράκτου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>R.</u>
					620e
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Epicur.
				<u>Ep.</u>
				2p.40U.
			</span></i>, al. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>5.</b> metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνάγκης στερραῖς δ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					1052
				</span></i>
			 (anap.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τελεσφόροις δίναις κυκλούμενον κέαρ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					997
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.).</div>
